Add 3-arg zone_device_page_init() detection probe.

Linux v7.x changed zone_device_page_init() from a 1-argument exported
symbol (void zone_device_page_init(struct page *)) to a 3-argument form:

  void zone_device_page_init(struct page *page,
                             struct dev_pagemap *pgmap,
                             unsigned int order)

The existing probe calls zone_device_page_init(NULL) which fails on v7.3
because the function now requires three arguments.  The flag is therefore
never set and kcl_mm.h re-declares zone_device_page_init with the old 1-arg
prototype, conflicting with the kernel's 3-arg declaration in memremap.h
(included transitively by hmm.h -> mm.h).

Add a fallback probe that tries the 3-arg form and, on success, sets both
HAVE_ZONE_DEVICE_PAGE_INIT and the new HAVE_ZONE_DEVICE_PAGE_INIT_3ARGS.

--- a/amd/dkms/m4/zone_device_page_init.m4
+++ b/amd/dkms/m4/zone_device_page_init.m4
@@ -12,6 +12,20 @@
 			], [zone_device_page_init], [mm/memremap.c], [
 				AC_DEFINE(HAVE_ZONE_DEVICE_PAGE_INIT, 1,
 					[zone_device_page_init() is available])
+		], [
+			dnl #
+			dnl # v7.x: zone_device_page_init() gained pgmap + order args
+			dnl #
+			AC_KERNEL_TRY_COMPILE_SYMBOL([
+					#include <linux/memremap.h>
+				], [
+					zone_device_page_init(NULL, NULL, 0);
+				], [zone_device_page_init], [mm/memremap.c], [
+					AC_DEFINE(HAVE_ZONE_DEVICE_PAGE_INIT, 1,
+						[zone_device_page_init() is available])
+					AC_DEFINE(HAVE_ZONE_DEVICE_PAGE_INIT_3ARGS, 1,
+						[zone_device_page_init() takes pgmap+order args])
+			])
 		])
 	])
 ])
